    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema (which generates `OwnerDto.getOwnerSegment()`/`setOwnerSegment()`), documenting the `<TIER>_<AREA>` format and its four allowed values.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` plus an `ownerSegment(Owner)` method that composes the value:\n   - **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD` (reusing the existing household-capped `membershipLevel`).\n   - **AREA**: `METRO` when `Localities.regionOf(owner.getCustomerCode())` is a known region (`NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`), else `REGIONAL` (reusing the existing locality derivation).\n\nI kept the field as a plain `String` to match the other computed fields (`locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`), avoiding a nested generated enum type in the MapStruct expression.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class) is green \u2014 both new cases (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown-region owner) pass, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
